author ai
group features/cli
note path-rm <name> [index]: with an index, delete that one step; its children move up to its parent, and every index after it shifts down by one. Without an index, delete the whole path, which is refused while any step in another path links to it, and the error lists each linking step so they can be unlinked first. There is no undo; the map's history is the version control of the repo.

